class creation:

class Class_Name{
 [properties]
 [methods]
 .....
 }

object creation:
$object_name = new Class_Name()

-------------------------------------------------------
We can add the "public" keyword before properties or methods inside the class. To access them outside of the class.
example:
<?php 

class Fruit {

	//properties
	public $name = "Fruit name";

	public function getName(){
		return "This is a fruit function";
	}

}
Now accessing them in the object:
//object
$mango = new Fruit();

echo $mango->name."<br>";

echo $mango->getName();
Here we use the object name, then the (->) sign, then the property (pulbic variable) or method(public function) name. 
